# Two input arms (sites 1 to 5 and 6 to 10) meet at site 11; the output arm runs from 11 to 16. The two pulses must arrive within a few photon lifetimes of each other: a coincidence detector.
# Reference: the same network integrated independently (complex arithmetic, LSODA).
title Weak junction, second input 10 photon lifetimes late
sites 16
path 1 5 kappa=0.06
path 6 10 kappa=0.06
path 11 16 kappa=0.06
link 5 11 kappa=0.03
link 10 11 kappa=0.03
kick 1 amplitude=2
kick 6 time=10 amplitude=2
run 1200
expect total 10
expect last 91.64954 0.003
expect count 1 1
expect arrival 1 12.96038 0.003
expect peak 1 58.059000 2e-4
expect count 3 1
expect arrival 3 48.19735 0.003
expect peak 3 56.713444 2e-4
expect count 4 1
expect arrival 4 65.46561 0.003
expect peak 4 56.690864 2e-4
expect count 6 1
expect arrival 6 22.96038 0.003
expect peak 6 58.059000 2e-4
expect count 8 1
expect arrival 8 58.19555 0.003
expect peak 8 56.714725 2e-4
expect count 9 1
expect arrival 9 75.50210 0.003
expect peak 9 56.675973 2e-4
